ginal Star Wars saga but in the  quirky platforming style the weapons and  gadgets used are varied and plentiful  and there's even a movie which sits  alongside if you become more invested  than you first thought oh the developer  behind this one insomnia  are currently making the ps4 version of  spider-man so now is a good time to  sample their work on the ps3 is mighty  number 9 which is also a cross by title  so play it on your ps4 if you like  mighty number 9 is the successor to  Megaman in every single way except  officially created by Megaman supremo  Keiji Inafune a this game is a 2.5 D  action platformer with a focus on speedy  combat the lead character is called beck  running through nine stages which can be  selected in any order the player desires  the story isn't plentiful but as a  starting point a computer virus has  caused Beck's  robot friends to go rogue and Megaman is  here to put things right  did I say Megaman I mean back of course  are you gonna try it out of interest  will you play it on ps4 or ps3 the  second title on ps3 is a game which came  out on the ps2 and was re-released with  improved graphics  The Legend of K anniversary edition it's  another action-adventure title with lots  of platforming elements thrown in for  good measure the story focuses around K  a bit of a hothead martial arts student  think of it like an angsty teenage  version of Kung Fu Panda and you're  pretty much on point  back in 2010 The Legend of K received  favorable reviews but eight years on it  kind of feels a little dated let me know  your thoughts if you download this one  on the Vita this month are two games  which can be played on your ps4 first up  is Claire extended Curt which is our  horror title for the month it's  essentially a 2d side-scroller with very  mixed reviews you fill the shoes of  Claire who makes a typical horror film  error and takes a wrong turn down a dark  passage leading to echoey corridors and  abandoned rooms the panic Claire feels  impacts the game and in nightmare mode  she can even die from fear itself the  decisions you make on the way to the  ending impact that ending so expect to  play multiple times to see all the  possible ending cinematics and finally  on Vita and ps4 is bomb Busters I'm  super excited by this one as it's  essentially super Bomberman from the  Super Nintendo days this is so  old-school and is  your time especially in a party scenario  as you attempt to blow up your friends  from the safety of your own couch as  long as the host is playing on ps4 and  both Vita and ps4 users can match up and  fight it's usually a case of  what-you-see-is-what-you-get  but believe me it's far more appealing  once your competitive edge kicks in I  could only find a couple of reviews for  this one and one was from our friends  over at push square who awarded it 60  out of 100 so there we have it six games  on offer during March with 5  downloadable TRPs for I could get used  to this for me I need to play bomb  Busters and I promised myself I'll  finally finish blood-borne but what  about you what floats your boat I'd love  to know what you think I imagine from  PlayStation grenade it's been a pleasure  as always  I'll see you next time
 

